PianoBluetooth is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). Level 1 (a read-only survey) as a kext; the GENI UART
plans, the H4 framing and the QCA vendor codec with the controller set-up sequence as host-tested portable headers. What it takes from
other work, and from where:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoUsbHost/PianoUsbHost.cpp (sha256 344da37e70682f579b6c0915ab5ac2e38183b17334b1ed0d883c7d5d6c453415): the kext's shape
    (probe gate on the boot argument, a survey thread, the post-mortem stage word, MMIO pages mapped on demand and loaded with an
    explicit ldr, the SPMI windows and the observer channel as the only store, one summary property), re-written for this driver;
    its decodePin / pullName copied into this namespace (GeniUart.h).
  package/PianoUsbHost/tests/usbhost_host.cpp (sha256 2e80c61089a79764f546bed763a4978299421d8d310cf7e08dd012edb9dd656c): the
    register-model harness (Soc, CHECK), re-used in tests/bt_host.cpp.
  package/PianoWifi/WifiSurvey.h (sha256 41a9703bf079dfd4f86fe5073399c788725d43e7dc0ad4306b36ffd16c9aa219): surveySmmu (read-only
    stream-match scan) re-expressed for one stream in GeniUart.h; the hardware-gated branch rule (piano-wifi-hwcg) taken as
    piano-bt-hwcg. PianoWifi itself is not modified and not linked against.
  package/PianoPower/SpmiObserver.h (sha256 4805d4fb7af91c210d75b9791e125f3789b7671e895afe6f80af27a36a849b07): included, not
    copied (-I package/PianoPower): the arbiter, the APID of a PPID with its owner, the observer read.

UniXNU-sheng (unixnu-research/UniXNU-sheng, BSD-2-Clause-Patent; SM8550 + WCN7850, Bluetooth hardware-verified on iPadOS 27 there),
facts and design only, no code:
  porting.toml (sha256 8f3d462ea12a78e90ca6ee8ed182e3f6573178841589305b0a49142631598894), area "bluetooth": the same QUP2 SE6 at
    0x898000 with INTID 493, wrapper 0x8c0000 and stream 0x423 on SM8550; 3.2 Mbit/s from a 51.2 MHz source at 16x oversampling;
    the macOS 27.3 (26C5035r) outcome (controller up, a patched bluetoothd opened /dev/cu.BLTH, its initialisation stopped at a
    Broadcom vendor command); WcnPower's model of the shared rails (independent Wi-Fi and Bluetooth ownership, the last owner
    releases; Bluetooth-only start-up without the PCIe NoC vote); pairing keys need the keychain.
  reports/ipados27-bluetooth-startup.md: GENI UART protocol 2 (revision 0x204) and QUP 0x30090000 read on SM8550.
  package/WcnPower.h (sha256 2ae8cda83623ca7370f6bfcbe3f86eb48bc5be5d3433cabfe313a36021850039): the shape of the shared power
    helper specified for PianoWifi in docs/drivers/bluetooth.md section 6 (one ownership vote per radio, idempotent until put).
  package/BluetoothProbe.cpp (sha256 2ae33391a94eadcb1f84dc13d1d4f33369cf91509d029aa0367ff45cbada8386): read for the bring-up
    order (clocks, pins, BT_EN, the 32 KiB DMA window through a bypass bank, the RX wake); its SM8550 pins and TLMM BT_EN are not
    piano's.
  dts/sheng.dts (sha256 7407181ec4c2a6207b039e2aa88869f70a414eaa35d0cacc231b41b69e041130): the ADT bluetooth node bluetoothd looks
    for (device_type and name "bluetooth", transport-encoding 1, transport-speed 3200000).

